What is the full form of GLS?
AI Overview
GLS has several full forms depending on the context, most commonly General Logistics Systems (a parcel delivery company), Gujarat Law Society (an Indian educational group), or General Lighting Service (referring to standard light bulbs); it can also stand for Generalized Least Squares in statistics or be part of the Mercedes-Benz GLS SUV's name, derived from German words meaning "off-road vehicle" and relating to the S-Class. 
Here are the most frequent meanings:
General Logistics Systems (GLS): A major international parcel delivery service operating in Europe, the US, and Canada, owned by International Distribution Services. 
Gujarat Law Society (GLS): A large educational organization in Gujarat, India, that includes GLS University and various colleges. 
General Lighting Service (GLS): A traditional, pear-shaped light bulb, often with B22 bayonet or E27 Edison screw fittings. 
Generalized Least Squares (GLS): A statistical method for linear regression analysis, especially useful with correlated errors. 
Mercedes-Benz GLS: In this context, "G" is for Geländewagen (off-road vehicle), "L" is a linkage, and "S" signifies it's the SUV equivalent of the S-Class sedan, per Mercedes-Benz nomenclature, says the Wikipedia article on the Mercedes-Benz GLS. 
